<!-- MEANING OF AYIN -->
<section class="section surface-page">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="meaning">
      <div class="reveal">
        <svg class="eye-mark" viewBox="0 0 260 260" role="img" aria-label="The AYiN eye mark">
          <circle class="ring" cx="130" cy="130" r="126"></circle>
          <circle class="ring" cx="130" cy="130" r="98" opacity="0.7"></circle>
          <ellipse cx="130" cy="130" rx="120" ry="62" fill="none" stroke="var(--line-gold)" stroke-width="1.2"></ellipse>
          <circle class="iris" cx="130" cy="130" r="46"></circle>
          <circle class="pupil" cx="130" cy="130" r="17"></circle>
          <line class="scan" x1="130" y1="130" x2="130" y2="8" stroke-dasharray="3 9"></line>
          <circle cx="130" cy="130" r="3" fill="var(--accent-fill-hover)"></circle>
        </svg>
        <figure class="photo-card surface-card reveal" data-d="1">
          <image-slot slug="skyscrapers" sizes="(min-width: 900px) 440px, calc(100vw - 80px)" loading="lazy"></image-slot>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow reveal"><span class="sec-index">01</span> &nbsp;The name</span>
        <h2 class="h2 reveal" data-d="1" style="margin-top:18px">AYiN means <span class="italic-accent">the eye.</span></h2>
        <p class="reveal" data-d="2">In the languages of the ancient Near East, <span class="lead-word">ayin</span> is the eye — perception, insight, the faculty of seeing what others miss. It is the right name for what we do.</p>
        <p class="reveal" data-d="3">Entering the United States is rarely defeated by a weak product. It is defeated by misreading the market — the regional nuance, the buying culture, the partner who looks right but isn't. We are the eye that reads it clearly, before you commit.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- STAT BAND -->
<section class="surface-alt">
